<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in thin trade as arrivals were very poor, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Farmers and traders are creating stock to ensure better prices, they said. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell 100 rupees per tonne on increased selling against limited demand. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down on limited exports demand at higher level. Soymeal yellow was $300-301 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $115-116 per tonne in export and was 3,950-4,000 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. The undertone was easy.</p>
